# Line endings.
#
# ── WHY THIS FILE EXISTS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Git for Windows installer sets `core.autocrlf=true` in the machine-level
# config. Left alone, that gives every file a CRLF working copy on checkout,
# which contradicts `.editorconfig` (`end_of_line = lf`) and makes
# `pnpm format:check` fail on a fresh clone, because Prettier is configured with
# `endOfLine: "lf"`. A checkout-dependent failure like that is reported as a
# formatting problem and is actually a line-ending problem, which wastes an
# afternoon.
#
# Declaring the intent here overrides the machine setting, so all three office
# workstations and any Linux CI get identical bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# .editorconfig specifies CRLF for PowerShell. Windows PowerShell 5.1 is also
# unreliable with LF-only script files containing non-ASCII characters.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
